      "writtenOn": "2026-02-02T19:09:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would be fine with having this being build flag controlled, but lean towards it not being.\n\nThe equivalent implementation for DXC isn\u0027t build flag controlled. You can control if DXC is built and used, but the actual options and logic in the fuzzer isn\u0027t gated on building DXC, so you can in theory provide your own DXC (which may or not be used).\n\nI think for Vulkan being able to build this without it being tied to building Mesa I think is more valuable, since there are other Vulkan implementations that might of interest in the future to test via this code path.\n\nWe could have a seperate build flag that is like TINT_BUILD_VULKAN_FUZZING, that is defaulted to what ever the build Mesa flag is, unless you override it. That in theory would allow for one to build the fuzzers without needing to build the vulkan loader, but I am not sure of if that is a case we really care about?\n\n(My initial implementation had this validation logic in a different file behind a build flag, but that was causing me needing to link in the Vulkan libraries into Tint itself so I moved it out to the fuzzer specific source file. So the dependency on vulkan should be isolated to building the fuzzer binaries. Though I think it should be relatively simple to implement a build flag if we want one.)",
      "parentUuid": "4493272e_8cf02a07",
      "revId": "dee72348b6d699afff9c5bc2ca7c3dbf4f086743",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
