        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-02T19:09:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding of the Mesa code (at a high-level) is that the SPIRV to NIR conversion is run as part of vkCreateShaderModule, performing basic translation and validation, which should be the same for all Mesa based drivers. The conversion from NIR to the GPU specific ISA may be deferred to later, since that is where heavy weight operations like optimization run.\n\nWhen running the fuzzer locally I have seen the coverage log messages getting into LLVM code in Mesa, so I am pretty sure we are hitting the to NIR conversion (and possibly beyon) for lavapipe.\n\n(Mapping onto the Tint design, vkCreateShaderModule should be doing the equilavent of lowering to core IR, and the raising to backend IR may be deferred or run at the same time depending on the specific implementation)\n\n(We may need/want to in the future add more calls, possibly controlled via flags to exercise further into the drivers of interest, but I think for a first step, I think this reaches to were we expect).",
      "parentUuid": "985e831d_6417a691",
      "revId": "dee72348b6d699afff9c5bc2ca7c3dbf4f086743",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
